{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Transfer Learning\n",
    "\n",
    "**Learning Objectives:** Understand pre-trained models, feature extraction vs fine-tuning, use Keras Applications, and build custom classifiers on top of pre-trained architectures."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Transfer Learning Concept\n",
    "\n",
    "Transfer learning leverages knowledge from a model pre-trained on a large dataset (e.g., ImageNet with 1.2M images) and adapts it to a new task.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why transfer learning works:**\n",
    "- Early layers learn general features (edges, textures, shapes)\n",
    "- Later layers learn task-specific features\n",
    "- A model trained on ImageNet has already learned excellent visual representations\n",
    "\n",
    "**Two main approaches:**\n",
    "\n",
    "| Approach | Freeze | Train | When to Use |\n",
    "|----------|--------|-------|-------------|\n",
    "| **Feature Extraction** | All base layers | Only new classifier | Small dataset, similar domain |\n",
    "| **Fine-Tuning** | Some early layers | Top layers + classifier | Larger dataset, different domain |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import tensorflow as tf\n",
    "from tensorflow import keras\n",
    "from tensorflow.keras import layers\n",
    "from tensorflow.keras.applications import VGG16, ResNet50, EfficientNetB0, MobileNetV2\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Keras Applications — Available Pre-trained Models\n",
    "\n",
    "| Model | Parameters | Depth | Top-1 Acc (ImageNet) | Speed |\n",
    "|-------|-----------|-------|---------------------|-------|\n",
    "| VGG16 | 138M | 16 | 71.3% | Slow, large |\n",
    "| ResNet50 | 25.6M | 50 | 76.0% | Good balance |\n",
    "| EfficientNetB0 | 5.3M | — | 77.1% | Fast, efficient |\n",
    "| MobileNetV2 | 3.5M | — | 71.8% | Very fast, mobile |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load VGG16 pre-trained on ImageNet (without top classifier)\n",
    "base_model = VGG16(\n",
    "    weights='imagenet',\n",
    "    include_top=False,  # exclude the classifier\n",
    "    input_shape=(224, 224, 3)\n",
    ")\n",
    "base_model.summary()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Feature Extraction Approach\n",
    "\n",
    "Freeze the base model and add a new classifier on top."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Feature extraction: freeze base model\n",
    "base_model.trainable = False  # freeze all layers\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add custom classifier on top\n",
    "inputs = keras.Input(shape=(224, 224, 3))\n",
    "x = base_model(inputs, training=False)  # inference mode\n",
    "x = layers.GlobalAveragePooling2D()(x)\n",
    "x = layers.Dropout(0.2)(x)\n",
    "x = layers.Dense(128, activation='relu')(x)\n",
    "outputs = layers.Dense(10, activation='softmax')(x)\n",
    "\n",
    "feature_extraction_model = keras.Model(inputs, outputs)\n",
    "feature_extraction_model.compile(\n",
    "    optimizer=keras.optimizers.Adam(learning_rate=0.001),\n",
    "    loss='categorical_crossentropy',\n",
    "    metrics=['accuracy']\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Trainable weights:\", len(feature_extraction_model.trainable_weights))\n",
    "feature_extraction_model.summary()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Prepare a small subset of CIFAR-10 as a proxy (resized to 224x224)\n",
    "(x_train, y_train), (x_test, y_test) = keras.datasets.cifar10.load_data()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Use only 1000 samples for speed\n",
    "x_train_small = x_train[:1000]\n",
    "y_train_small = y_train[:1000]\n",
    "x_test_small = x_test[:200]\n",
    "y_test_small = y_test[:200]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Resize to 224x224 (VGG16 required size)\n",
    "x_train_resized = tf.image.resize(x_train_small, (224, 224)).numpy()\n",
    "x_test_resized = tf.image.resize(x_test_small, (224, 224)).numpy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Normalize (VGG16 expects specific preprocessing)\n",
    "from tensorflow.keras.applications.vgg16 import preprocess_input\n",
    "x_train_pp = preprocess_input(x_train_resized)\n",
    "x_test_pp = preprocess_input(x_test_resized)\n",
    "\n",
    "y_train_cat = keras.utils.to_categorical(y_train_small, 10)\n",
    "y_test_cat = keras.utils.to_categorical(y_test_small, 10)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Preprocessed: {x_train_pp.shape}, labels: {y_train_cat.shape}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Train the feature extraction model\n",
    "hist_fe = feature_extraction_model.fit(\n",
    "    x_train_pp, y_train_cat,\n",
    "    batch_size=32,\n",
    "    epochs=10,\n",
    "    validation_data=(x_test_pp, y_test_cat),\n",
    "    verbose=1\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "fe_acc = feature_extraction_model.evaluate(x_test_pp, y_test_cat, verbose=0)[1]\n",
    "print(f\"Feature extraction test accuracy: {fe_acc:.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Fine-Tuning Approach\n",
    "\n",
    "Unfreeze some top layers of the base model to adapt features to the new task."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Fine-tuning: unfreeze top layers of VGG16\n",
    "base_model.trainable = True\n",
    "\n",
    "# Freeze early layers, unfreeze later ones\n",
    "for layer in base_model.layers[:15]:  # freeze first 15 layers\n",
    "    layer.trainable = False\n",
    "for layer in base_model.layers[15:]:  # unfreeze remaining\n",
    "    layer.trainable = True\n",
    "\n",
    "# Recompile (important: must recompile after changing trainable)\n",
    "feature_extraction_model.compile(\n",
    "    optimizer=keras.optimizers.Adam(learning_rate=1e-5),  # lower LR for fine-tuning\n",
    "    loss='categorical_crossentropy',\n",
    "    metrics=['accuracy']\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Trainable layers:\")\n",
    "for i, layer in enumerate(base_model.layers):\n",
    "    if layer.trainable:\n",
    "        print(f\"  Layer {i}: {layer.name}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Fine-tune the model\n",
    "hist_ft = feature_extraction_model.fit(\n",
    "    x_train_pp, y_train_cat,\n",
    "    batch_size=32,\n",
    "    epochs=5,\n",
    "    validation_data=(x_test_pp, y_test_cat),\n",
    "    verbose=1\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "ft_acc = feature_extraction_model.evaluate(x_test_pp, y_test_cat, verbose=0)[1]\n",
    "print(f\"Fine-tuning test accuracy: {ft_acc:.4f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Compare with feature extraction\n",
    "print(f\"\\nFeature extraction: {fe_acc:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Fine-tuning:       {ft_acc:.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": {
    "## 5. When to Use Feature Extraction vs Fine-Tuning\n",
    "\n",
    "| Scenario | Dataset Size | Similarity | Approach |\n",
    "|----------|-------------|-----------|----------|\n",
    "| New dataset is small, similar to original | Small | High | Feature extraction |\n",
    "| New dataset is large, similar to original | Large | High | Fine-tune (few layers) |\n",
    "| New dataset is small, different from original | Small | Low | Feature extraction + strong reg |\n",
    "| New dataset is large, different from original | Large | Low | Fine-tune (many layers) |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Rule of thumb:**\n",
    "1. First do feature extraction (freeze base, train classifier)\n",
    "2. If performance plateaus, try fine-tuning with a small LR"
   }
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Quick comparison: different pre-trained models as feature extractors\n",
    "model_configs = {\n",
    "    'ResNet50': (ResNet50, keras.applications.resnet.preprocess_input, (224, 224)),\n",
    "    'EfficientNetB0': (EfficientNetB0, keras.applications.efficientnet.preprocess_input, (224, 224)),\n",
    "    'MobileNetV2': (MobileNetV2, keras.applications.mobilenet_v2.preprocess_input, (224, 224))\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "for name, (arch, preproc, target_size) in model_configs.items():\n",
    "    # Resize and preprocess\n",
    "    x_pp = preproc(tf.image.resize(x_train[:500], target_size).numpy())\n",
    "    y_pp = keras.utils.to_categorical(y_train[:500], 10)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Build feature extractor\n",
    "    base = arch(weights='imagenet', include_top=False, input_shape=(*target_size, 3))\n",
    "    base.trainable = False\n",
    "\n",
    "    model = keras.Sequential([\n",
    "        base,\n",
    "        layers.GlobalAveragePooling2D(),\n",
    "        layers.Dense(10, activation='softmax')\n",
    "    ])\n",
    "    model.compile(optimizer='adam', loss='categorical_crossentropy', metrics=['accuracy'])\n",
    "    model.fit(x_pp, y_pp, epochs=5, verbose=0)\n",
    "    acc = model.evaluate(x_pp, y_pp, verbose=0)[1]\n",
    "    print(f\"{name:20s}: {acc:.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Data Augmentation with Transfer Learning\n",
    "\n",
    "Always use augmentation when fine-tuning to prevent overfitting."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Data augmentation + transfer learning pipeline\n",
    "data_augmentation = keras.Sequential([\n",
    "    layers.RandomFlip('horizontal'),\n",
    "    layers.RandomRotation(0.1),\n",
    "    layers.RandomZoom(0.1),\n",
    "    layers.RandomContrast(0.1),\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Build model with augmentation\n",
    "base = MobileNetV2(weights='imagenet', include_top=False, input_shape=(224, 224, 3))\n",
    "base.trainable = False\n",
    "\n",
    "inputs = keras.Input(shape=(224, 224, 3))\n",
    "x = data_augmentation(inputs)\n",
    "x = preprocess_input(x)\n",
    "x = base(x, training=False)\n",
    "x = layers.GlobalAveragePooling2D()(x)\n",
    "x = layers.Dropout(0.2)(x)\n",
    "outputs = layers.Dense(10, activation='softmax')(x)\n",
    "\n",
    "aug_model = keras.Model(inputs, outputs)\n",
    "aug_model.compile(optimizer='adam', loss='categorical_crossentropy', metrics=['accuracy'])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Transfer learning model with augmentation ready.\")\n",
    "print(f\"Non-trainable weights: {len(base.non_trainable_weights)}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Interview Problems\n",
    "\n",
    "### Problem 1: Classify Custom Image Dataset Using Transfer Learning\n",
    "\n",
    "Given a custom dataset of 5 flower classes (100 images each), build a classifier using MobileNetV2 feature extraction. Preprocess images to the required input size. Achieve >85% validation accuracy.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Problem 2: Compare Feature Extraction vs Fine-Tuning\n",
    "\n",
    "Train two models on the same dataset — one using feature extraction only, one using fine-tuning. Compare:\n",
    "- Training time\n",
    "- Final accuracy\n",
    "- Overfitting tendency\n",
    "\n",
    "### Problem 3: Progressive Unfreezing\n",
    "\n",
    "Implement progressive unfreezing: train classifier (frozen base) → unfreeze last block → unfreeze more blocks. Show accuracy improves at each step."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Solution: Problem 3 — Progressive unfreezing\n",
    "def progressive_unfreeze(model, base_model, x_train, y_train, x_val, y_val, epochs_per_stage=5):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Gradually unfreeze layers and retrain.\"\"\"\n",
    "    history = []\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Stage 1: train only classifier\n",
    "    base_model.trainable = False\n",
    "    model.compile(optimizer=keras.optimizers.Adam(1e-3),\n",
    "                  loss='categorical_crossentropy', metrics=['accuracy'])\n",
    "    h = model.fit(x_train, y_train, epochs=epochs_per_stage,\n",
    "                   validation_data=(x_val, y_val), verbose=0)\n",
    "    acc = model.evaluate(x_val, y_val, verbose=0)[1]\n",
    "    history.append(('Classifier only', acc))\n",
    "    print(f\"Classifier only: {acc:.4f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Stage 2: unfreeze last 20% of base layers\n",
    "    base_model.trainable = True\n",
    "    for layer in base_model.layers[:int(len(base_model.layers) * 0.8)]:\n",
    "        layer.trainable = False\n",
    "    model.compile(optimizer=keras.optimizers.Adam(1e-5),\n",
    "                  loss='categorical_crossentropy', metrics=['accuracy'])\n",
    "    h = model.fit(x_train, y_train, epochs=epochs_per_stage,\n",
    "                   validation_data=(x_val, y_val), verbose=0)\n",
    "    acc = model.evaluate(x_val, y_val, verbose=0)[1]\n",
    "    history.append(('Top 20% unfrozen', acc))\n",
    "    print(f\"Top 20% unfrozen: {acc:.4f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Stage 3: unfreeze all\n",
    "    for layer in base_model.layers:\n",
    "        layer.trainable = True\n",
    "    model.compile(optimizer=keras.optimizers.Adam(1e-6),\n",
    "                  loss='categorical_crossentropy', metrics=['accuracy'])\n",
    "    h = model.fit(x_train, y_train, epochs=epochs_per_stage,\n",
    "                   validation_data=(x_val, y_val), verbose=0)\n",
    "    acc = model.evaluate(x_val, y_val, verbose=0)[1]\n",
    "    history.append(('All unfrozen', acc))\n",
    "    print(f\"All unfrozen: {acc:.4f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    return history\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Progressive unfreezing function defined.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Transfer learning** leverages pre-trained models (ImageNet) for new tasks\n",
    "- **Feature extraction** freezes the base model and trains only the classifier\n",
    "- **Fine-tuning** unfreezes some base layers with a low LR for task-specific adaptation\n",
    "- **Keras Applications** provides VGG16, ResNet50, EfficientNet, MobileNet, and more\n",
    "- **When to use:** Feature extraction for small datasets; fine-tuning for larger datasets\n",
    "- **Key steps:** freeze base → add classifier → train classifier → (optional) unfreeze & fine-tune\n",
    "- Always recompile after changing trainable status\n",
    "- Use lower LR (1e-5 to 1e-4) for fine-tuning to avoid destroying pre-trained features"
   ]
  }
 ],
